# Coverage gates enforced by CI (see CONTRIBUTING.md § Testing).
# Ratchet UP only, never down. Keep a little slack under the measured figure so
# an unrelated PR cannot fail on run-to-run jitter.
#
# Measured 2026-10-29 (cargo llvm-cov --workspace, main.rs excluded):
#   lines 86.34   regions 86.97   functions 86.50
#
# Branch coverage is NOT gated because it is not measured: branch counters need
# -Z coverage-options=branch, which is nightly-only and fails on the pinned
# stable toolchain. The functions figure is not branch coverage.
#
# Slack is sized in misses rather than points, because one miss moves each
# metric differently: one uncovered function costs 0.086 points (1163
# functions), one region 0.006 (16291 regions), one line 0.010 (9616 lines). The
# gates below hold roughly 4 functions / 20 regions / 5 lines of headroom.
#
# The lowest-covered code is the network edge (catalog-ingest fetch.rs and
# logos.rs, catalog-store's S3 path, catalog-api state.rs). Tests there are the
# cheapest way to raise these numbers.
lines=86.2
regions=86.8
functions=86.1
